    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1607" root="ايك" body-key="A">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيِكَ الأَرَاكُ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَيَكَ</span></b> , <i>The</i> [<i>trees called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اراك</span>
<i>became what is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْكَة</span> [n. un. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْكٌ</span>, q. v.];
as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">استأيك</span></b> . (K.) The former occurs in
poetry contracted into <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْكَ</span>. (ISd, Sgh.)

